WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.800
Westworld Season 3 explores a new world.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.330
The robot Dolores has escaped the Westworld
park, and enters the real human world, in

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:17.110
the year 2058 . This season’s almost like
a reboot, with a new setting, new characters,

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:21.980
and new style, but with the same themes of
technology, freedom and control.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.820
It’s also got Death Grips now.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.769
The premiere begins with a beach – just
like Season 2 begins on a beach, and Season

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:31.939
1 ends on a beach.

00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:36.760
Teddy once said that “Where the mountains
meet the sea”, the water will “wash the

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.590
past” off you, so “you can start again”
. Westworld is washing away the chaos of Season

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:46.290
2, and starting a new story in a new world.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.990
Or maybe it’s just a fckin beach [let’s
not overthink it].

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.060
Jerry is a rich asshole in a Chinese mansion.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.860
He’s angry cause he’s an investor in the
Westworld parks, and news just broke that

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:02.630
a hundred people died in the parks, when Dolores
and the hosts went on a rampage last season.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:09.280
Jerry is rude and controlling to his wife
Eunice, so Jerry is instantly dislikeable.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.689
We see futuristic technology – like there
are holograms you can see with special glasses.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:18.270
And there are high-tech drugs called limbic
tabs.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:22.149
People have implants on the roof of their
mouth, and when you put in a tab, it sends

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:25.600
a digital code to your brain to change your
mood.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.219
The Westworld website says available flavours
include “Zen Garden”, “Agenda Achiever”,

00:01:31.219 --> 00:01:32.369
and “Impulse”.

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:38.030
Jerry’s mansion has smart-home technology,
like an Alexa robot voice that controls the

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.229
place.

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:44.549
This whole human world is run by machines,
which makes it vulnerable to machines like

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:50.490
Dolores . Dolores comes in the night, and
hacks the smart-home system, turning off the

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.759
oxygen to knock everyone out.

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:57.170
Jerry tries to get help and the system says
“I'm afraid I can't do that” , which is

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:03.319
what HAL 9000 says in 2001: A Space Odyssey
. Dolores confronts Jerry, and says she met

00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:07.590
Jerry before – he once came to the Westworld
park and Dolores.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.789
“Don't you remember?”

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:14.290
Dolores says – “After everything we've
shared” . That’s just like what William

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:20.010
says to Dolores in Season 1 . But this time
Dolores is the powerful one, and the human

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.620
is the helpless.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.500
Dolores knows all about Jerry.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.670
Because last season, she went to the Forge
, which records data on all the memories and

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:33.950
DNA and minds of everyone who visits Westworld
. So Dolores knows that Jerry murdered his

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:39.670
last wife . She straps the hologram glasses
onto Jerry, to project images of his crime

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:44.019
– haunting him like the ghost of Christmas
past.

00:02:44.019 --> 00:02:48.800
Dolores steals money from Jerry, and takes
data about a company called Incite , which

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.489
runs all the data tech in the world.

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:56.930
Dolores says her goal is “The origin of
a new species” – she wants the robot hosts

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.860
of Westworld to become their own free people
– which means she’ll have to deal with

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:02.860
humanity.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.790
But Dolores says she doesn’t want to hurt
anyone, unless they try to hurt her.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.790
Because Dolores has “hurt so many people”
already . Last season, Dolores killed lots

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.470
of humans and hosts who may have been innocent.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:21.450
Her brutality drove her lover Teddy to suicide,
which seems to have changed Dolores’ mind.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.430
She doesn’t wanna kill unless she has to.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:29.490
So when Jerry tries to kill her, she uses
a hologram in the glasses to trick Jerry into

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.180
dying in his pool.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.989
She tells Jerry’s wife Eunice that she’s
set her free from her murderous husband.

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:42.290
So Dolores is no longer an evil murderbot
taking revenge on the entire human species.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:47.519
Now she fights for justice and liberation,
freeing not only hosts, but oppressed humans

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:48.970
like Eunice.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:54.340
Dolores takes a swim in Jerry’s pool, which
could symbolise washing away her past sins,

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:00.830
and starting anew, just like Teddy said . The
title of this episode is Parce Domine, a Catholic

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:07.260
thing meaning “Spare, Lord, spare your people:
Be not angry with us forever” . Dolores

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:12.920
is less angry now – she’s more merciful
and just, like a benevolent god.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:18.290
This could make Dolores a much more sympathetic
character than she was last season.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.180
In Los Angeles, we meet Caleb.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:25.199
He’s the first average person we’ve met
in this series – all the park guests in

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:30.500
past seasons were rich tourists, corporate
types, technologists and sadists.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.740
Caleb’s just an ordinary guy, getting by
in LA in 2058.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:41.341
He works in construction – this shot refers
to a famous photo from 1930s New York . But

00:04:41.341 --> 00:04:47.020
Caleb works with a robot, and there’s driverless
cars, and all the city looks modern clean

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.030
and green.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:53.910
Caleb says technology has made some things
better – but Caleb feels trapped . His mother

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:59.410
is sick, apparently with dementia or something,
because she no longer recognises him.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.440
And he can barely afford her medical bills.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.259
So Caleb turns to crime – and there’s
an app for that.

00:05:05.259 --> 00:05:09.640
It’s called Rico, and it’s like Uber or
Taskrabbit for crime.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:15.030
Its algorithm offers jobs based on your location
and profile – burglary, delivery, grand

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.880
theft auto, murder.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:22.080
Everything’s anonymous, automatic, efficient,
and apparently untraceable – showrunner

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.620
Jonathan Nolan says it works on the blockchain,
like a Deep Web thing.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.780
And it’s gamified – you get points and
badges and “crime coins”, and rate people

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:35.660
on their performance, which affects which
jobs you can get, like star ratings in Uber.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:41.220
So Rico is a “parody” of our real-world
algorithmic “gig economy” . Caleb does

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.600
robberies and transport and stuff, but he
chooses not to do “personals” , meaning

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.030
he won’t do murder and kidnap and stuff.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:53.470
So Caleb’s a very sympathetic character
– he only does crime to pay his mum’s

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:54.470
medical bills.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:59.090
But Caleb feels trapped in a loop – these
shots of Caleb waking up each morning are

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.040
just like Dolores waking up in Season 1.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.860
Caleb takes a job robbing an ATM, just like
the host Hector robs the saloon in Season

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:07.860
1.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:12.551
Hector does the same robbery over and over
because his programming tells him to, just

00:06:12.551 --> 00:06:18.250
like Caleb does these Rico jobs, over and
over, cause its algorithm tells him to.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:23.560
Season 1 was about robots stuck in loops,
this season is about humans stuck in loops,

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.020
controlled by code.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.500
Caleb meets with some criminal buddies – Ash
and Giggles.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.270
Giggles is played by NFL player Marshawn Lynch,
and he’s got a sick mood shirt that changes

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.050
depending on how he feels.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:39.880
Ash has a device that blocks surveillance
and blasts Death Grips at max volume.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:45.509
So this is a stylish, cyberpunk dystopia – these
guys barely scrape by, but they look fine

00:06:45.509 --> 00:06:47.300
while they do it.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.240
The Westworld parks are run by the Delos corporation.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.560
They have a meeting, in the aftermath of the
massacre last season.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:59.000
And it’s run by Charlotte Hale, except we
know that’s not really Charlotte – last

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:05.259
season, Dolores killed Charlotte, and impersonated
her with Dolores’ brain in a Charlotte body.

00:07:05.259 --> 00:07:11.200
When Dolores left the park, she created a
new Charlotte – so whose brain is in there?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.379
Maybe it’s one of these five host brains
she took from the park.

00:07:15.379 --> 00:07:19.270
It can’t be just Dolores, cause we’ve
seen Dolores with this Charlotte last season

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.270
[and in trailers].

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:23.680
It’s not Teddy, cause Dolores left him behind
in the Sublime [Windows XP heaven].

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.740
It’s not Angela, cause she blew up in the
Cradle.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:29.199
It’s not Maeve, or Bernard.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:31.270
Maybe it could be Hector or Armistice?

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:36.879
Or there could be a twist, like maybe it’s
not a host at all, but a copy of a human,

00:07:36.879 --> 00:07:38.980
like the James Delos clone.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:43.669
Or it could be a totally new person, like
a host child.

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:48.229
Whoever this Charlotte is, she’s working
with Dolores to influence Delos – she takes

00:07:48.229 --> 00:07:52.789
the company private , and says to “resume
host production” – maybe Dolores wants

00:07:52.789 --> 00:07:58.270
to keep making hosts, so that her “new species”
can grow . Maybe she wants the parks to keep

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:03.330
running because she agrees with Ford, that
hosts need to suffer in the park before they

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.710
can become conscious , like Dolores did.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:11.250
To control the board, Charlotte needs approval
from another board member, who isn’t at

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.550
the meeting – this must be William.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:18.930
William owns Westworld, he’s the majority
shareholder . But for years, he’s not come

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:23.710
to meetings, preferring to spend his time
in the park . He must leave this “machine

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:28.379
shareholder” to vote on stuff for him, and
it agrees with Charlotte.

00:08:28.379 --> 00:08:31.199
Last time we saw [human] William, he was alive
in the park.

00:08:31.199 --> 00:08:35.710
But where is he now, and does he still control
this machine?

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:39.940
Maybe Charlotte is hacking this machine – like
Dolores hacks Jerry’s home.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:46.600
Either way, Charlotte takes control, and she
blames the whole Westworld massacre on Bernard

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.110
.
So Bernard is on the run.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:53.351
He’s left his old life behind for a simpler
one, like The Hound in Game of Thrones, with

00:08:53.351 --> 00:08:55.910
a very similar outfit.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:01.110
Bernard works on a farm, and he finds an injured
cow with flies buzzing round it.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:06.570
In Season 2, Dolores tells the story of some
cows getting an infection, spread by flies.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:09.930
Teddy says he’d protect and help the infected
cows.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:15.680
But Dolores said she’d kill the weak cows,
so the strong cows can live . So this continues

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:20.240
the theme of mercy versus survival – Parce
Dominem.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.529
Should the weak die so that the strong can
survive?

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:28.029
Should the weak humans die, so that the hosts
can grow and thrive?

00:09:28.029 --> 00:09:32.850
Bernard tries to help the hurt cow, but his
human boss sends it for slaughter – just

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:37.750
like humanity may be slaughtered, unless Dolores
is merciful.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:42.550
Inside the slaughterhouse, humans butcher
animals – just like hosts were butchered

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:46.100
in the Westworld park, in the “livestock”
section.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:51.839
Then Bernard talks to himself, in diagnostic
mode – he seems to have two distinct personalities.

00:09:51.839 --> 00:09:57.740
There’s the more human conscious side, and
the more robotic unconscious side – they

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:01.589
talk to each other, like Gollum and Smeagol
in Lord of the Rings.

00:10:01.589 --> 00:10:06.130
Bernard doesn’t trust his robo side – he
questions whether he’s been influenced by

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:12.240
Dolores . Cause this Bernard was created by
Dolores last season – maybe Dolores left

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:16.850
some backdoor to hack or control Bernard’s
subconscious mind.

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:21.320
Bernard’s identity and mental state have
always been complicated.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:27.420
Bernard is a host based on a human called
Arnold – Arnold Weber is an anagram of Bernard

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:28.420
Lowe.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:34.610
Now, Bernard uses a fake identity, Armand
Delgado – which is an anagram for Damaged

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.720
Arnold.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:42.550
So Armand is an alias of a copy of a copy
of a dead man – and each time he’s remade,

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:46.089
he’s changed, rearranged like the letters
of his name.

00:10:46.089 --> 00:10:49.550
So Bernard is all scrambled, and he’s struggling
to figure out who he is.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:55.260
Bernard is attacked by some workers who recognise
him as a fugitive – so Bernard lets out

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:01.110
his robo side, which is a powerful fighter
– it’s like Eddie Brock unleashing Venom.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:05.329
Bernard says that he’s trying to save the
human race from Dolores , but they don’t

00:11:05.329 --> 00:11:06.329
listen.

00:11:06.329 --> 00:11:10.340
So he’s forced to hurt the people he’s
trying to save, like that cow.

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:15.490
So like in previous seasons, Bernard’s story
is confusing, but at least everything seems

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:19.420
to be happening within one timeline again.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:24.959
Dolores goes to a fancy corporate event for
Incite, the tech company that runs the world’s

00:11:24.959 --> 00:11:25.959
data.

00:11:25.959 --> 00:11:31.060
Dolores has seduced the face of Incite, Liam
Dempsey, and is using him to get information

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.410
on the company.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:37.770
The party is full of wealth and luxury and
douchebags – Liam’s friend brags that

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:42.970
his drink is worth more than people earn in
a year . Meanwhile, Caleb can’t afford his

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:48.340
mum’s medical bills – so this is a deeply
unequal society, which is not so different

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.430
to reality.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.550
Showrunner Jonathan Nolan says this is what
the world might be like if we continue the

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:58.279
way we’re going – with a small number
of people holding even more of the wealth

00:11:58.279 --> 00:12:03.920
and power, controlling everyone else through
technology . Liam’s friend gets high and

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:09.110
says nothing is real, we’re all “living
in a simulation” man . It is a common theory

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:14.760
that the so-called real world in this show
is just another fake reality, or another park,

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:15.839
like Futureworld.

00:12:15.839 --> 00:12:21.199
But the showrunners are clearly interested
in exploring our reality, so having this guy

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:25.420
rant about simulations might be their way
of dismissing the theory and saying that this

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.149
is the real real world.

00:12:28.149 --> 00:12:32.610
Dolores says that a part of the brain called
the Nucleus accumbens evolved to make humans

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:38.079
believe in God, which is a loose interpretation
of the neuroscience, but there is evidence

00:12:38.079 --> 00:12:43.149
linking the nucleus accumbens to religious
experiences . So Dolores’ point is that

00:12:43.149 --> 00:12:47.930
believing that we’re inside someone’s
simulation is basically the same as believing

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:50.570
we’re in a world created by a God.

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:55.200
Either way, you’re just believing in a higher
power because that’s what our brains have

00:12:55.200 --> 00:13:01.570
evolved to believe – humans, like robots,
can only follow their code.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:07.480
Dolores sees Rehoboam, a computer that processes
all the data for the Incite corporation.

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:12.329
Its algorithm gives strategies that tell people
how to live – what you should buy, what

00:13:12.329 --> 00:13:18.250
job you should work, who you should date – Incite
offers “A path for everyone” . In Season

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:24.010
1, Dolores believed in “a path for everyone”
– but then she realised that was her programming,

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:29.820
trapping her in a loop of suffering . Humans
had been free, but now they’ve built technology

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:32.709
that traps them in loops as well.

00:13:32.709 --> 00:13:38.160
Dolores uses a sick cyberbike and spy-glasses
to listen in to a meeting between Liam and

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.660
an Incite person called Martel.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:45.630
She says someone has been accessing Rehoboam
, through Liam – so this probably means

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:49.160
Dolores got in by exploiting Liam’s access.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:54.560
Martel threatens to use Rehoboam’s data
to assassinate Liam . Liam admits to Dolores

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.760
that he has no real power at Incite.

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:02.899
The only person who controls Rehoboam is its
original architect – a mysterious guy called

00:14:02.899 --> 00:14:09.540
Serac . Liam implies that Serac may have murdered
Liam’s father, who was Serac’s business

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:15.769
partner . Dolores gets captured by Martin,
a hardarse fixer for Liam – Martin figured

00:14:15.769 --> 00:14:18.610
out that Dolores was using a fake identity.

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:24.779
So Martin uses Rico to hire someone to brings
some drugs to kill Dolores – and Caleb gets

00:14:24.779 --> 00:14:30.080
the delivery job . Martin injects Dolores
with the lethal drugs, but they do nothing,

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.230
cause she’s a robot.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:37.060
Dolores summons a driverless car, and inside
is a host copy of Martin.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.520
This whole thing is Dolores’ trap – like
with Jerry, she must have used data from the

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.570
Forge to predict and manipulate Martin.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.410
She kills Martin and replaces him with the
host Martin loyal to her.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:54.440
So with this Martin and the Charlotte, Delores
is using hosts to infiltrate powerful tech

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:59.560
companies, to take over the human world and
help the birth of the new host species.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:05.280
Martin’s men attack, and they have a shoot-out
in MacArthur Park – Dolores goes all Terminator

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.600
on their asses.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.140
As a robot, she’s fast, and tough.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:10.970
But she’s not invulnerable.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:15.500
She walks wounded into a tunnel, where Caleb
finds her.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:20.529
Caleb was once in the army with his mate Francis
– played by Kid Cudi.

00:15:20.529 --> 00:15:25.430
But something went wrong, Francis got killed,
and Caleb is traumatised.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:29.440
The army put him in a psych program, but instead
of a human therapist, he has to talk to a

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:35.480
chatbot with the voice and personality of
his dead friend like some Black Mirror shit.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:39.839
And this Francis-bot isn’t like the real
Francis – the bot encourages compliance

00:15:39.839 --> 00:15:44.440
with the system and ‘playing the game’,
when the real Francis was rebellious . So

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:49.940
Caleb rejects the bot and says he needs “someone
… real” – and that’s when he meets

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.040
Dolores.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:56.620
So the irony will be that the robot Dolores
is the realest person in Caleb’s life – cause

00:15:56.620 --> 00:16:01.709
unlike everyone else trapped in a loop, Dolores
follows her own plan.

00:16:01.709 --> 00:16:07.100
In Season 1, Dolores fell into the arms of
William, who became the Man in Black – William

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:10.600
taught her that humans are selfish and cruel.

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:14.160
Maybe Caleb will show Dolores that humans
can be good and selfless.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:19.760
Showrunner Jonathan Nolan says Caleb represents
“humanness and humility and kindness”

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:22.660
. But Caleb is still mysterious.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:27.360
He casually mentions that he’s been shot
in the head before , and his mother did say

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:33.069
he’s not her son . So there are theories
that Caleb is actually some robot replacement.

00:16:33.069 --> 00:16:38.670
Though that could undermine the whole human
good idea . But we’ve gotta question whether

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:43.250
this meeting of Dolores and Caleb really is
random chance.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.860
Caleb was brought to Dolores by a job on the
Rico app.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:51.550
Rico is meant to be untrackable, but it’d
be a cool twist if the crime app was actually

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:54.190
controlled by Incite.

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:59.389
The easiest way to prevent rebellion is to
make rebellion part of the system, right – like

00:16:59.389 --> 00:17:05.130
in the Matrix, when the One and Zion are actually
programmed by the machines, or like the prison

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.540
industry in the real world.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:12.110
Throughout the episode, we get these shots
where some system sees “divergence” and

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.460
anomalies in the places where Dolores and
Caleb go.

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:21.100
Maybe this is Rehoboam, seeing Dolores and
Caleb as flickers in the world’s data.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:26.080
Maybe Serac, who controls Rehoboam, deliberately
brings Caleb and Dolore together for some

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.170
higher plan.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:31.070
At the very least, Incite is fcking with Caleb.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:35.820
He interviews to get a better job , but gets
rejected by a company’s “strategy group”

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:40.780
. Rehoboam’s thoughts are called “Strategies”
– so it seems like Incite’s data is preventing

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.710
him from getting hired.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:48.770
Maybe cause Rehoboam is aware of his criminal
activity on Rico, or is listening to his anti-authority

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:51.770
[rebellious] attitudes in his calls with the
Francis-bot.

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:56.840
Or maybe it’s some arbitrary reason – the
point is that through data technology, humanity

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.100
has handed its freedom away to machines.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:06.780
So even outside the Westworld park, we can’t
be sure who’s in control and what’s real.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:11.640
Bernard takes a boat to the Westworld parks
– his map seems to confirm that the Westworld

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.050
is on an island in the South China Sea.

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:18.850
Bernard says he’s “looking for a friend”,
and after the credits, we see the friend he’s

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:19.980
looking for.

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:23.160
Maeve wakes up in an unfamiliar place.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.510
Last season, sacrificed herself to save her
daughter.

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:30.500
The techs Felix and Sylvester were told to
salvage her . And it looks like they’ve

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:37.540
put her in a new park – Warworld, a simulation
of Italy in the second world war . Bernard’s

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:43.020
goal is apparently to get Maeve’s help to
stop Dolores from destroying humanity . So

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:47.890
Maeve might finally leave Westworld and see
the real world for the first time.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:52.630
In Season 1, Maeve’s programmed narrative
said that she “Crossed the shining sea”

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:58.440
, to a “new world” – where she “can
be whoever the fuck” she wants . Now she’ll

00:18:58.440 --> 00:18:59.940
get to do that for real.

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:03.280
But first, she’ll kill some Ns.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:08.350
Westworld has a new intro sequence, that highlights
some of themes of the season.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:13.610
There’s a dandelion, with its florets traced
by geometric lines – like how the natural

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:19.110
world follows mathematical laws, and the human
mind can be described with lines of code.

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:24.430
There’s an eagle flying into a jet engine,
like Icarus at the sun – like how humanity

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:28.220
is destroying itself in the pursuit of technology.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:33.130
But the main imagery is of reflection – repetitions,
and symmetry.

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.910
Season One was about hosts controlled by code.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:38.500
Season Three is about humans controlled by
code.

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:42.840
Delores was powerless against humans, now
she's the powerful one.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:45.150
She meets Caleb, as she met William.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:49.730
Bernard worked on host livestock, now he works
on animal livestock.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:54.190
Images lines and phrases are repeated and
refracted in different situations.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:20:00.040
This is even reflected in the architecture
– all this glass, mirrors, water.

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:05.180
This shot also resembles the famous painting
The Creation of Adam, which appeared in Season

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.180
1.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:13.090
We see dividing cells, cause Dolores wants
the birth of a new host species . So there

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.190
is some optimism in this new intro.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:21.270
But the intro ends with the logo in bright
red – hinting that despite all the changes,

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:28.590
Westworld remains a bloody affair – violent
delights, violent ends.

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:34.730
The intro also shows Rehoboam, cause this
season is all about data and algorithms controlling

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.100
humanity.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:41.480
This might sound like a sci-fi idea, but big
tech has been using data to predict and control

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:46.540
us for years – and you can read all about
this in The Age of Surveillance Capitalism

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:52.630
by Shoshana Zuboff . It’s a deep exploration
of the systems that increasingly control our

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:57.870
lives, it’s at least as scary as anything
in Westworld, and it’s real.

